; Unused test code: show the room's attribute map, X resets
;
; Never executed and unreachable: it follows the RET of #R$96DE, nothing jumps or
; calls to $96F4 and no word in the image holds that address. Not part of the
; game; it looks like a debugging aid. What it would do (run in the simulator
; from the in-game snapshot): copies the empty-room attribute master copy
; ($5E00-$5FFF, 512 bytes) over the top two thirds of the attributes, fills the
; bitmap of the top two thirds ($4000-$4FFF) with $18 (a thin vertical bar in
; every cell), so the room's colour layout is shown without sprites or graphics.
; It then polls the keyboard half row CS-V (port $FEFE) forever; the X key (bit
; 2) jumps to $0000, which resets the machine. Observed: with X pressed the run
; reaches PC=$0000 after a frame or two, without X it stays in the polling loop.
; .
; Hardware: writes screen bitmap and attributes; reads keyboard port $FEFE.
@label=ShowAttrMap
c$96F4 LD HL,$5E00   ;
 $96F7 LD DE,$5800   ;
 $96FA LD BC,$0200   ;
 $96FD LDIR          ;
 $96FF LD HL,$4000   ;
 $9702 LD DE,$4001   ;
 $9705 LD BC,$0FFF   ;
 $9708 LD (HL),$18   ;
 $970A LDIR          ;
@isub=LD BC,KEYROW_CS_V
 $970C LD BC,$FEFE   ;
*$970F IN A,(C)      ;
 $9711 BIT 2,A       ;
 $9713 JP Z,$0000    ;
 $9716 JR $970F      ;
